You may not directly or indirectly monetize the Licensed Material or any derivative work based upon it without separate permission from the applicable copyright holders.

This prohibition applies even when copies of, or access to, the software itself are provided without charge.

Prohibited Monetization includes, but is not limited to:

- selling copies, builds, downloads, physical media, or access;
- charging subscriptions or membership fees for access, development, updates, or support;
- Patreon, Ko-fi, GitHub Sponsors, or similar recurring funding solicited in connection with the Licensed Material or a derivative work;
- donations solicited or received for the development, maintenance, distribution, hosting, or continued availability of the Licensed Material or a derivative work;
- crowdfunding campaigns connected to the Licensed Material or a derivative work;
- sponsorships connected to the Licensed Material or a derivative work;
- advertising revenue generated by, incorporated into, or specifically associated with the Licensed Material or a derivative work;
- paid early access;
- premium or supporter-only builds;
- paid feature access;
- affiliate or referral revenue incorporated into or promoted through the Licensed Material or a derivative work; and
- paid support, hosting, distribution, or other commercial services whose value is substantially based upon the Licensed Material or a derivative work.

Having unrelated employment, operating a business, maintaining an unrelated donation page or Patreon, receiving unrelated sponsorships, or having other sources of income does not by itself violate this license.

The restriction applies when Monetization is connected to, promoted through, used to fund, or substantially based upon the Licensed Material or a derivative work.

Independent journalism, commentary, criticism, reviews, video coverage, academic discussion, or other activities that do not require permission under copyright law are not restricted by this license merely because the person performing those activities receives income.

