## 9. Source Availability for Distributed Derivatives

If you distribute executable, object-code, or other non-source forms of a modified version or derivative work covered by this license, you must also make the complete Corresponding Source for the covered derivative available to every recipient at no additional charge.

The Corresponding Source must be provided either:

1. together with the distributed work; or
2. through a publicly accessible location clearly identified in documentation accompanying the distributed work.

The Corresponding Source must include the preferred source form for making modifications to the covered portions of the work, together with build files, scripts, configuration files, and other project material reasonably necessary to build and modify those covered portions.

The Corresponding Source must remain available for at least as long as you distribute or otherwise make the corresponding non-source form available.

The Corresponding Source provided under this section must itself be distributed under this license.

This section does not require disclosure of independent material that is not derived from, based upon, or otherwise legally part of a derivative work of the Licensed Material.

